# Connected vehicles / telematics — MASSIVE FAN-IN, tiny fan-out.
#
# Millions of vehicles publishing telemetry to their own topic; a handful of
# backend consumers read through ONE $share group. Huge connection count,
# LOW per-client rate, QoS 1 (trip data loss matters).
#
# The per-client rate is deliberately 1 msg/s. emqtt-bench's QoS 1 publish is
# SYNCHRONOUS (one PUBACK round trip per client at a time), so a high per-client
# rate makes the LOAD GENERATOR the limit, not the broker — measured 2026-08-26:
# at 10 msg/s x 100K clients the brokers sat at 39-44% CPU while 97% of
# publishes ran late. At 1 msg/s the ack round trip has room and the number is
# the BROKER's.
LANES=B
LANE_B_QOS=1
LANE_B_FANOUT=0
LANE_B_PUBS_OVERRIDE=100000
LANE_B_SUBS_OVERRIDE=100
LANE_B_PUB_CONTAINERS=5
LANE_B_SUB_CONTAINERS=1
LANE_B_RUNGS_OVERRIDE="100000"
# Sweep the workload's own axis by overriding the population per run:
#   LANE_B_PUBS_OVERRIDE=25000|50000|100000|200000 (with the rung = pubs x 1/s)
# Tuning levers: MQTTD_RECEIVE_MAXIMUM, MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS,
#   MQTTD_DURABLE_SESSIONS on/off, MQTTD_MAX_INFLIGHT_MESSAGES.
